{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "643d5db6-a5b0-4672-870b-2adfbd5db4c9",
    "name": "Quartile Assessment",
    "description": "Stores API (Q1, App Service) and Products Functions (Q2, Azure Functions).\n\n**How to run**\n- `production` environment: run the whole collection in order. It creates a company, a store and a product, checks the error cases and cleans everything up at the end.\n- `staging` environment: only the Products Functions staging slot exists, so run just the **2. Products Functions** and **4. Cleanup - products** folders. `storeId` points to the seeded staging store.\n\nKeys are not committed. Fill `apiKey` (Stores API, `X-Api-Key` header) and `functionsKey` (Functions, `x-functions-key` header) in the environment before running.\n\nNote: the first request after a while can take a few seconds (serverless database + Functions cold start).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Stores API",
      "auth": {
        "type": "apikey",
        "apikey": [
          {
            "key": "key",
            "value": "X-Api-Key",
            "type": "string"
          },
          {
            "key": "value",
            "value": "{{apiKey}}",
            "type": "string"
          },
          {
            "key": "in",
            "value": "header",
            "type": "string"
          }
        ]
      },
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{storesUrl}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{storesUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "description": "Anonymous. Also checks the database connection (it can be slow on the first call because the serverless DB may be paused)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"is healthy\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.eql(\"Healthy\"));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Without API key -> 401",
